      "key": {
        "uuid": "13b89fa0_a3c2b81f",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/index/change/ChangeIndexer.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 456,
      "author": {
        "id": 1072905
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-27T11:49:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`deleteAllForProject` is an **interface method**, not an implementation [1].\nIt is then overridden by the `LuceneChangeIndex`, which provides a specific implementation for it.\n\nI had this at a higher level, so that it would be send regardless the index implementation flavour we had.\n\nHaving said that, the Lucene-specific implementation is the _only_ implementation that takes care of this bulk deletion, so perhaps you\u0027re right, and we should move it down the stack.\n\nWere you suggesting to fire notifications *within* the Lucene-specific implementation?\n\n[1] https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/changes/84/501384/2/java/com/google/gerrit/extensions/events/ChangeIndexedListener.java#53",
      "parentUuid": "3b730327_1ebdc496",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 456,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 456,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "0408a7ae3c8308cc53df2220e9ef7e895db4db9c",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0ff2bc83_fc24d8ee",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/index/change/ChangeIndexer.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 456,
      "author": {
        "id": 1072905
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-27T14:59:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also, if we were to emit the notification from within the Lucene implementation, we would possibly end up with multiple events, since this is executed *per write index*.\n\n```\n    for (ChangeIndex i : getWriteIndexes()) {\n      i.deleteAllForProject(projectName);\n    }\n```",
      "parentUuid": "13b89fa0_a3c2b81f",
